1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,290
Listen to a talk in a neuroscience class.

2
00:00:02,290 --> 00:00:02,612
Man:

3
00:00:02,612 --> 00:00:05,991
Let’s talk a little about language acquisition,

4
00:00:05,991 --> 00:00:09,290
which is the process by which humans learn to understand and use language.

5
00:00:09,290 --> 00:00:12,647
There are two main types of language acquisition:

6
00:00:12,647 --> 00:00:17,070
first language acquisition and second language acquisition.

7
00:00:17,070 --> 00:00:25,114
First language acquisition occurs naturally and with relative ease during early childhood, through interaction with family

8
00:00:25,114 --> 00:00:27,000
and the surrounding environment.

9
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:31,337
Children are able to pick up their native language quickly due to their innate

10
00:00:31,337 --> 00:00:37,240
linguistic capabilities, a concept supported by the linguist Noam Chomsky’s theory of Universal Grammar.

11
00:00:37,240 --> 00:00:42,983
Universal Grammar suggests that the ability to acquire language is innate to humans

12
00:00:42,983 --> 00:00:47,080
and that all human languages share a common underlying structure.

13
00:00:47,080 --> 00:00:54,163
Second language acquisition, on the other hand, often requires more conscious effort and formal education

14
00:00:54,163 --> 00:00:56,230
and typically happens later in life.

15
00:00:56,230 --> 00:01:03,592
Several factors influence the ease and success of second language acquisition, including exposure to

16
00:01:03,592 --> 00:01:06,100
the language, age, and motivation.

17
00:01:06,100 --> 00:01:15,293
Motivation, in particular, plays a crucial role—highly motivated individuals are more likely to engage actively with the language

18
00:01:15,293 --> 00:01:17,080
and persist in their learning efforts.

19
00:01:17,080 --> 00:01:19,028
Age is also significant;

20
00:01:19,028 --> 00:01:24,369
according to the critical period hypothesis, there is an optimal window in early childhood

21
00:01:24,369 --> 00:01:27,220
during which language acquisition occurs most easily.

22
00:01:27,220 --> 00:01:32,030
After this period, acquiring a new language can be more challenging.

23
00:01:32,030 --> 00:01:37,436
Understanding these processes helps educators and linguists develop effective teaching methods

24
00:01:37,436 --> 00:01:38,280
and language learning tools.
